--[[
	Net
	---
	Replicates cars between hub users through the relay (relay/server.js).

	  * On build/rebuild the car's *structure* is sent once: wheel layout, every visual
	    piece (role, wheel corner, mesh, texture, scale, size, colour, material, offset
	    from the body) and the engine sound pack.
	  * While it exists the car streams an 81-byte *state*: chassis CFrame, velocities,
	    pedals, gear, rpm and per-wheel suspension offset, steer, camber, spin and slip.
	    20 Hz while anything moves, slower at rest.
	  * Incoming data is decoded defensively (sizes, ranges, NaN, asset allow-list) and
	    handed to Replica, which rebuilds and interpolates the other cars locally.

	Binary layouts are documented in relay/server.js and must stay in sync with it.
	Transport: the executor's WebSocket API. In Studio, Net.loopback() mirrors your own
	car back as a fake peer for testing.
]]

